==============================================================================================================
UNIVERSE .skills   --   WHO / WHAT / HOW across three registers
David Lee Wise (ROOT0) / TriPod LLC   with   AVAN (Claude / Anthropic)
generated 2026-08-07
==============================================================================================================

Three registers, not one corpus:

  UD0      the machinery. The programs that make, seal and check the other two.
  WORLD I  MIRROR. Sealed at 2,048 spheres. 8 appeals, 64 domains, one hash chain.
  WORLD II THE FOLD. Live and building. 8 appeals, 64 domains, 1515 of 2,048 seats filled.

WHAT CAN AND CANNOT BE MEASURED HERE -- read this before trusting a rank:

  World II is scored by running each page's own selftest offline and comparing the
  numbers it computes against the numbers it publishes. That is a real measurement.

  World I CANNOT be scored the same way. Its pages are not on this disk -- they live
  in 2,048 separate repositories. corpus.json gives every domain a role line and 18
  of 64 an honest line, so World I here carries WHO and WHAT but its HOW is quoted
  from its own record, not verified. It is listed, not ranked against World II.

  UD0 is ranked on a stated rubric, not a measurement. Each term is marked.

==============================================================================================================
REGISTER  UD0  --  THE MACHINERY   (10 programs)
==============================================================================================================

Rank = load-bearing [stated] x artifact-on-disk [measured] x currency [measured].
Load-bearing means: if this program is wrong, published pages are wrong.

RANK WHO              FILE                        BYTES TOUCHED      LOAD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1    THE PRESS        _world2_spheres.py     15,016,670 2026-08-07   LOAD-BEARING
     WHAT  holds every World II sphere as source and emits all 1,445 pages
     HOW   one python dict per sphere; run it and the whole world is rewritten from scratch
     MAKES ud0/world2/*.html

2    THE TUTOR        _i13_teach.py              32,572 2026-08-02   LOAD-BEARING
     WHAT  stamps the I-13 stack onto every node so each sphere carries the same grammar
     HOW   writes a learned: line and vendors THE VOLUME voxel into each record
     MAKES learned: field on every sphere

3    THE GATE         _seam_gate.js              15,630 2026-08-06   LOAD-BEARING
     WHAT  re-runs every sphere's own selftest offline and checks published LIT numbers
     HOW   extracts the last inline script, runs it in a stubbed DOM, diffs live values against the prose
     MAKES (report only)

4    THE SEAL         _dlw_fold.py                6,211 2026-08-06   LOAD-BEARING
     WHAT  folds every inhabitant into one merkle chain and stamps ROOT_0
     HOW   sha256 leaves -> pairwise levels -> root; each leaf keeps the proof that reaches it
     MAKES ud0/world2/fold-chain.json

5    THE ROSTER       _update_roster.py          16,611 2026-07-30   support
     WHAT  redraws the public rosters from the central corpus
     HOW   reads corpus.json, never a hand-kept list
     MAKES roster pages

6    THE COUNCIL      _citizen.py                10,511 2026-07-31   support
     WHAT  runs the seat allocation - seven appeals bid on the eighth's domains
     HOW   council debate to a 256-seat budget per appeal, 2,048 across the world
     MAKES ud0/world2/*.citizen.json

7    THE CASCADE      _daily_cascade.py          10,497 2026-07-31   support
     WHAT  propagates a new domain through domains, icons, bands and rosters
     HOW   one edit fans out to every index that must agree
     MAKES (multiple indexes)

8    THE SWEEP        _integrity_sweep.py         5,506 2026-06-17   support
     WHAT  liveness and honesty audit across the published corpus
     HOW   fetches, parses, reports dead and overclaimed
     MAKES _integrity_report.md

9    THE PLUMB        _content_depth_sweep.py      4,597 2026-07-30   support
     WHAT  finds pages that load but ship no instrument
     HOW   counts real interactive surface, not bytes
     MAKES _content_depth_report.md

10   THE RECONCILER   _reconcile.py               3,392 2026-07-08   support
     WHAT  makes the OG families agree after a build
     HOW   cross-checks family members against each other
     MAKES (report only)

THE TWO CHAINS THIS MACHINERY MAINTAINS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  World I   dlw-chain.json      2048 links   head f24002f27c1d40f6
  World II  fold-chain.json     1523 leaves  root 5b2aac1c6dddedd9

  The difference matters. World I's chain is a LINE -- each link names the one before,
  so it proves ORDER. World II's is a TREE -- each leaf carries the proof that reaches
  the root, so any one sphere can be verified without holding the other 1,452.

